hi i'm michael morris i am the deputy  electoral officer for the infrared city  council and i'm going to give you a  quick run through about the by-election  that's coming up  so a by-election happens where you've  got a sitting counsellor  who resigns during the term of council  within the three years  meaning that there's a vacancy created  amongst the council table so rather than  12 councillors we have 11.  we can't have 11 councillors because the  number is set during our representation  review process of how many councillors  we have on each  council so from chiropractic we have 12  plus the mayor  which means that if we have a vacancy we  have to fill it so anyone throughout new  zealand can  stand and become a candidate all you  have to do is  be enrolled to vote somewhere within new  zealand which given we've just had the  general election means most people  should be and then you all you have to  do is be nominated by two people who are  residents of  the embargo city district  so that includes bluff in case people  are wondering voting begins on the 26th  of january which is when new zealand  post starts  delivering the postal ballots if you  don't receive your postal ballot you're  free to come in and make a  special vote so just come into the civic  administration building or the bluff  service centre  the election day is the 17th of february  and poland closes at 12 pm
 

